{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc | sed -n '1160,1385p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc | sed -n '1385,1575p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/pipeline_test.cljc | sed -n '1,420p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1160\t\n  1161\t(def ^:private record-attributes\n  1162\t  \"Every attribute a projected record entity may carry: the declared\n  1163\t   dimension slots, markers included.\"\n  1164\t  (into #{} (map first) dimension-slots))\n  1165\t\n  1166\t\n  1167\t(defn- slot-shape-ok?\n  1168\t  \"Whether `v` fits the descriptor `type` on a projected record: the\n  1169\t   deterministic gate the storage reader hashes behind, so a wrongly\n  1170\t   typed slot — :yin.debruijn/bound 5, a numeric child ref — diagnoses\n  1171\t   :unsupported-value instead of reaching host arithmetic inside the\n  1172\t   hash recomputation.\"\n  1173\t  [type v]\n  1174\t  (cond\n  1175\t    (= :canonical type) (canonical-value? v)\n  1176\t    (= :keyword type) (keyword? v)\n  1177\t    (= :symbol type) (symbol? v)\n  1178\t    (= :string type) (string? v)\n  1179\t    (= :bool type) (or (true? v) (false? v))\n  1180\t    (= :int64 type) (and (number? v) (= :int64 (numeric-class v)))\n  1181\t    (or (= :ref type) (= :hash type)) (and (string? v)\n  1182\t                                           (re-matches #\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\" v))\n  1183\t    (and (vector? type) (= :tuple (first type)))\n  1184\t    (and (vector? v)\n  1185\t         (= (count v) (count (rest type)))\n  1186\t         (every? true? (map slot-shape-ok? (rest type) v)))\n  1187\t    (vector? type) (and (vector? v) (every? #(slot-shape-ok? :ref %) v))\n  1188\t    :else false))\n  1189\t\n  1190\t\n  1191\t(defn- projected-slots-of\n  1192\t  \"The projected slots one §2 grammar attribute becomes (§4): the binder\n  1193\t   :yin/params becomes :arity, an occurrence's :yin/name becomes one of\n  1194\t   :bound or :free, and every other attribute keeps its name under\n  1195\t   :yin.debruijn.\"\n  1196\t  [attr]\n  1197\t  (case attr\n  1198\t    :yin/params [:yin.debruijn/arity]\n  1199\t    :yin/name [:yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free]\n  1200\t    [(keyword \"yin.debruijn\" (name attr))]))\n  1201\t\n  1202\t\n  1203\t(def ^:private record-slots\n  1204\t  \"Per node type, every slot its projected record may carry besides\n  1205\t   :yin.debruijn/hash — derived from `node-grammar`, so the reader's\n  1206\t   grammar and the walk's are one table. The preimage frames slots by\n  1207\t   type tag, not name, so this check is what keeps a slot renamed within\n  1208\t   one type (:free to :key on a :variable, :arity to :buffer) from\n  1209\t   passing under a valid address.\"\n  1210\t  (into {}\n  1211\t        (map (fn [[tag {:keys [scalars children]}]]\n  1212\t               [tag (into #{:yin.debruijn/type}\n  1213\t                          (mapcat (comp projected-slots-of first))\n  1214\t                          (concat scalars children))]))\n  1215\t        node-grammar))\n  1216\t\n  1217\t\n  1218\t(def ^:private optional-record-slots\n  1219\t  \"The record slots a writer may leave absent: :macro? (only a true one\n  1220\t   is written) and :bound/:free, of which a :variable carries exactly\n  1221\t   one.\"\n  1222\t  #{:yin.debruijn/macro? :yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free})\n  1223\t\n  1224\t\n  1225\t(defn- canonical-spelling?\n  1226\t  \"Whether `v` is already its own canonical spelling — the form\n  1227\t   `canonical-value` gives every stored scalar. Exact, never =: Dart's\n  1228\t   1 == 1.0 and Clojure's = across a set's members would pass a stored\n  1229\t   1.0 whose address is 1's, and the reader would hand back a record no\n  1230\t   writer produces. A JS number carries one spelling per value, so every\n  1231\t   in-domain number is canonical there.\"\n  1232\t  [v]\n  1233\t  (case (canonical-class v)\n  1234\t    (:nil :bool :bytes) true\n  1235\t    :int64 #?(:cljs true :default (int? v))\n  1236\t    ;; :cljd first: the ClojureDart host pass also reads :clj\n  1237\t    :double #?(:cljd true :clj (instance? Double v) :cljs true)\n  1238\t    :string (= v (normalize-nfc v))\n  1239\t    (:keyword :symbol) (and (or (nil? (namespace v))\n  1240\t                                (= (namespace v) (normalize-nfc (namespace v))))\n  1241\t                            (= (name v) (normalize-nfc (name v))))\n  1242\t    :map (every? (fn [[k x]] (and (canonical-spelling? k) (canonical-spelling? x))) v)\n  1243\t    (:set :vector :list) (every? canonical-spelling? v)\n  1244\t    false))\n  1245\t\n  1246\t\n  1247\t(defn- check-record\n  1248\t  \"The reader's record gate, after every slot fits its declared shape:\n  1249\t   the record's type is a grammar type, it carries exactly its type's\n  1250\t   slots (a :variable exactly one of :bound/:free, a :macro? only when\n  1251\t   true), and every scalar is its canonical spelling. Everything here is\n  1252\t   what the writer already guarantees, so no minted hash moves.\"\n  1253\t  [record e]\n  1254\t  (let [tag (get record :yin.debruijn/type)\n  1255\t        allowed (or (get record-slots tag)\n  1256\t                    (throw (ex-info \"Projected record has an unknown node type\"\n  1257\t                                    {:rule :unknown-node-type, :type tag, :entity e})))\n  1258\t        present (disj (set (keys record)) :yin.debruijn/hash)]\n  1259\t    (doseq [slot present]\n  1260\t      (when-not (contains? allowed slot)\n  1261\t        (throw (ex-info \"Projected slot is outside its node type's grammar row\"\n  1262\t                        {:rule :unknown-attribute,\n  1263\t                         :attribute slot,\n  1264\t                         :type tag,\n  1265\t                         :entity e}))))\n  1266\t    (doseq [slot allowed]\n  1267\t      (when-not (or (contains? present slot)\n  1268\t                    (contains? optional-record-slots slot))\n  1269\t        (throw (ex-info \"Projected record lacks a required slot\"\n  1270\t                        {:rule :missing-slot, :slot slot, :type tag, :entity e}))))\n  1271\t    (when (and (= :variable tag)\n  1272\t               (not= 1 (count (filter #(contains? present %)\n  1273\t                                      [:yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free]))))\n  1274\t      (throw (ex-info \"A projected :variable carries exactly one of :bound and :free\"\n  1275\t                      {:rule :missing-slot,\n  1276\t                       :slot [:yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free],\n  1277\t                       :type tag,\n  1278\t                       :entity e})))\n  1279\t    (doseq [[slot _type role] dimension-slots\n  1280\t            :when (and (= :scalar role) (contains? record slot))]\n  1281\t      (let [v (get record slot)]\n  1282\t        (when-not (and (canonical-spelling? v)\n  1283\t                       ;; the writer spells a false :macro? by its absence\n  1284\t                       (not (and (= :yin.debruijn/macro? slot) (false? v))))\n  1285\t          (throw (ex-info \"Projected scalar is not its canonical spelling\"\n  1286\t                          {:rule :noncanonical-value,\n  1287\t                           :slot slot,\n  1288\t                           :value v,\n  1289\t                           :entity e})))))))\n  1290\t\n  1291\t\n  1292\t(defn datoms->projected\n  1293\t  \"The d5 storage adapter's read half (§4): projected datoms back to\n  1294\t   {:fingerprint h, :records {h record}} — the inverse of\n  1295\t   `projected->datoms` over the record set (the resolved :root graph is\n  1296\t   the named side's, never rebuilt here). Every entity must carry its\n  1297\t   :yin.debruijn/hash; exactly one entity is the :yin.debruijn/root\n  1298\t   marker and its hash is the fingerprint; every slot must fit its\n  1299\t   declared shape BEFORE its hash is recomputed — a wrongly typed slot\n  1300\t   diagnoses :unsupported-value, never a host exception; each record must\n  1301\t   then be one its writer can produce — its type's grammar slots only\n  1302\t   (:unknown-node-type, :unknown-attribute, :missing-slot), every scalar\n  1303\t   in its canonical spelling (:noncanonical-value) — because the\n  1304\t   preimage frames slots by type tag, not name, and equal encodings do\n  1305\t   not mean equal spellings; child refs must resolve to records;\n  1306\t   :yin.debruijn/operands must be one vector of hashes. Each record is\n  1307\t   re-hashed and a disagreement is a\n  1308\t   :hash-mismatch diagnostic — content addressing is verified at this\n  1309\t   boundary, never trusted. t, m, and other namespaces are layout,\n  1310\t   ignored.\"\n  1311\t  [datoms]\n  1312\t  (let [datoms (vec datoms)\n  1313\t        index (index-frame \"yin.debruijn\" datoms)\n  1314\t        markers (into []\n  1315\t                      (comp (filter #(= :yin.debruijn/root (nth % 1)))\n  1316\t                            (filter #(true? (nth % 2)))\n  1317\t                            (map first))\n  1318\t                      datoms)\n  1319\t        _ (when-not (= 1 (count markers))\n  1320\t            (throw (ex-info \"Projected datoms have not exactly one root marker\"\n  1321\t                            (if (zero? (count markers))\n  1322\t                              {:rule :missing-root}\n  1323\t                              {:rule :multiple-roots, :roots markers}))))\n  1324\t        root-e (first markers)\n  1325\t        records (reduce-kv (fn [recs e facts]\n  1326\t                             (let [h (or (when (contains? facts :yin.debruijn/hash)\n  1327\t                                           (get facts :yin.debruijn/hash))\n  1328\t                                         (throw (ex-info\n  1329\t                                                  \"Projected entity carries no :yin.debruijn/hash\"\n  1330\t                                                  {:rule :missing-hash, :entity e})))\n  1331\t                                   record (dissoc facts :yin.debruijn/root)]\n  1332\t                               (doseq [a (keys record)]\n  1333\t                                 (when-not (contains? record-attributes a)\n  1334\t                                   (throw (ex-info\n  1335\t                                            \"Unknown :yin.debruijn/* attribute on a projected record\"\n  1336\t                                            {:rule :unknown-attribute,\n  1337\t                                             :attribute a,\n  1338\t                                             :entity e}))))\n  1339\t                               (when-not (and (string? h)\n  1340\t                                              (re-matches #\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\" h))\n  1341\t                                 (throw (ex-info \"Projected hash is not 64 lowercase hex\"\n  1342\t                                                 {:rule :malformed-hash,\n  1343\t                                                  :hash h,\n  1344\t                                                  :entity e})))\n  1345\t                               (doseq [[slot type role] dimension-slots\n  1346\t                                       :when (and (not= :marker role)\n  1347\t                                                  (contains? record slot))]\n  1348\t                                 (when-not (slot-shape-ok? type (get record slot))\n  1349\t                                   (throw (ex-info\n  1350\t                                            \"Projected slot value does not fit its declared type\"\n  1351\t                                            {:rule :unsupported-value,\n  1352\t                                             :slot slot,\n  1353\t                                             :value (get record slot),\n  1354\t                                             :entity e}))))\n  1355\t                               (check-record record e)\n  1356\t                               (if (contains? recs h)\n  1357\t                                 (throw (ex-info\n  1358\t                                          \"Two entities claim one projected hash\"\n  1359\t                                          {:rule :duplicate-fact,\n  1360\t                                           :attribute :yin.debruijn/hash,\n  1361\t                                           :entity e}))\n  1362\t                                 (do (when-not (= h (node-hash (slot-encodings record)))\n  1363\t                                       (throw (ex-info\n  1364\t                                                \"Projected record does not hash to its address\"\n  1365\t                                                {:rule :hash-mismatch,\n  1366\t                                                 :hash h,\n  1367\t                                                 :entity e})))\n  1368\t                                     (assoc recs h record)))))\n  1369\t                           {}\n  1370\t                           index)\n  1371\t        fingerprint (get-in index [root-e :yin.debruijn/hash])]\n  1372\t    (doseq [[h record] records\n  1373\t            [slot type role] dimension-slots\n  1374\t            :when (and (= :child role) (contains? record slot))]\n  1375\t      (let [refs (if (and (vector? type) (= :ordered-vector (first type)))\n  1376\t                   (let [v (get record slot)]\n  1377\t                     (when-not (vector? v)\n  1378\t                       (throw (ex-info\n  1379\t                                \"Projected :yin.debruijn/operands is not an ordered vector\"\n  1380\t                                {:rule :unsupported-value,\n  1381\t                                 :slot slot,\n  1382\t                                 :value v,\n  1383\t                                 :hash h})))\n  1384\t                     v)\n  1385\t                   [(get record slot)])]\n  1385\t                   [(get record slot)])]\n  1386\t        (doseq [ref refs]\n  1387\t          (when-not (contains? records ref)\n  1388\t            (throw (ex-info \"Projected child hash resolves to no record\"\n  1389\t                            {:rule :dangling-ref, :hash ref, :via h, :slot slot}))))))\n  1390\t    {:fingerprint fingerprint, :records records}))\n  1391\t\n  1392\t\n  1393\t;; =============================================================================\n  1394\t;; D4: the dao.stream forward adapter (§6)\n  1395\t;; =============================================================================\n  1396\t\n  1397\t(def forward-default-options\n  1398\t  \"Defaults for `forward-step`: one read or one write per call, terminal\n  1399\t   gap policy — the same shape `dao.stream.forward` gives its copier.\"\n  1400\t  {:batch-budget 1})\n  1401\t\n  1402\t\n  1403\t(defn forward-initial-state\n  1404\t  \"The state `forward-step` consumes: the input cursor, the current\n  1405\t   graph frame (the §2 accumulation the next :yin/root marker closes),\n  1406\t   and pending projected output. The fact index, scope stack, and\n  1407\t   occurrence memo of §1 live inside the pure per-frame projection —\n  1408\t   the index resets with every frame (§2) — so no step carries them.\"\n  1409\t  [cursor]\n  1410\t  {:cursor cursor, :frame [], :pending []})\n  1411\t\n  1412\t\n  1413\t(defn- forward-budget-ok?\n  1414\t  \"A batch budget is a positive integer: 0 would answer :continue with no\n  1415\t   progress under every host cadence, forever, so it is invalid input\n  1416\t   like any other non-positive or non-integer budget.\"\n  1417\t  [budget]\n  1418\t  (and (integer? budget) (pos? budget)))\n  1419\t\n  1420\t\n  1421\t(defn- forward-terminal-status\n  1422\t  \"The terminal status of a source-side outcome, named as\n  1423\t   `dao.stream.forward` names its copier's.\"\n  1424\t  [outcome]\n  1425\t  (case outcome\n  1426\t    :dao.stream/end :source-ended\n  1427\t    :dao.stream/gap :source-gap\n  1428\t    :dao.stream/cursor-mismatch :source-cursor-mismatch\n  1429\t    :dao.stream/invalid-cursor :source-invalid-cursor\n  1430\t    :dao.stream/transport-error :source-transport-error\n  1431\t    :transport-error))\n  1432\t\n  1433\t\n  1434\t(defn- forward-destination-status\n  1435\t  [outcome]\n  1436\t  (case outcome\n  1437\t    :dao.stream/closed :destination-closed\n  1438\t    :dao.stream/invalid-value :destination-invalid-value\n  1439\t    :dao.stream/transport-error :destination-transport-error\n  1440\t    :transport-error))\n  1441\t\n  1442\t\n  1443\t(defn- forward-result\n  1444\t  [state status forwarded outcome diagnostic]\n  1445\t  (cond-> (assoc state :status status :forwarded forwarded)\n  1446\t    outcome (assoc :outcome outcome)\n  1447\t    diagnostic (assoc :diagnostic diagnostic)))\n  1448\t\n  1449\t\n  1450\t(def ^:private internal-rules\n  1451\t  \"Diagnostic rules only the projection's own code can produce — a\n  1452\t   defect in it, never in its input.\"\n  1453\t  #{:missing-record})\n  1454\t\n  1455\t\n  1456\t(defn exception-diagnostic\n  1457\t  \"The terminal classification of a throw from forward-step's read path:\n  1458\t   an ex-info carrying an input diagnostic — a keyword :rule outside\n  1459\t   `internal-rules` — is invalid input, its own ex-data; anything else\n  1460\t   (an internal rule, ex-data without a :rule, a plain host error, an\n  1461\t   Error) is an internal defect: :internal-error with the message, and\n  1462\t   the ex-data under :data when there is any — never mislabeled input\n  1463\t   and never host-divergent.\"\n  1464\t  [t]\n  1465\t  (let [data (ex-data t)\n  1466\t        rule (when (map? data) (get data :rule))]\n  1467\t    (if (and (keyword? rule) (not (contains? internal-rules rule)))\n  1468\t      {:status :invalid-input, :diagnostic data}\n  1469\t      {:status :internal-error,\n  1470\t       :diagnostic (cond-> {:rule :internal-error, :message (ex-message t)}\n  1471\t                     data (assoc :data data))})))\n  1472\t\n  1473\t\n  1474\t(defn forward-step\n  1475\t  \"§6's forward interpretation: read :yin/* datoms from `source` at the\n  1476\t   state's cursor, frame at the :yin/root marker — projecting there —\n  1477\t   and emit the projected d5 tuples to `destination`. One call performs\n  1478\t   at most :batch-budget units of work, a unit being one read or one\n  1479\t   pending write; the state thread is the only state there is (§1: no\n  1480\t   atom, callback, timer, registry, or clock).\n  1481\t\n  1482\t   Statuses: :continue (budget spent, work may remain) and :retry\n  1483\t   (source blocked, or destination full with pending output kept —\n  1484\t   pending writes are explicit and retried only by the host's cadence)\n  1485\t   are non-terminal; terminal statuses are :source-ended (input ended\n  1486\t   on a closed frame), :partial-frame (input ended with :yin/* datoms\n  1487\t   no marker closes — §2's diagnostic, its frame under :diagnostic),\n  1488\t   :invalid-input (a malformed datom or a projection diagnostic, the\n  1489\t   ex-data under :diagnostic; or a :batch-budget that is not a positive\n  1490\t   integer, :rule :invalid-budget, before any work), :internal-error (a non-diagnostic\n  1491\t   throwable from the read path — an internal defect, never mislabeled\n  1492\t   input), the source transport defects (:source-gap,\n  1493\t   :source-cursor-mismatch, :source-invalid-cursor,\n  1494\t   :source-transport-error, :transport-error), and the destination\n  1495\t   defects (:destination-closed, :destination-invalid-value,\n  1496\t   :destination-transport-error). Every result carries :forwarded — the\n  1497\t   count of THIS call's writes, as dao.stream.forward's does — and\n  1498\t   carries :outcome whenever the last transport operation produced one,\n  1499\t   including the blocked/full outcome a :retry hands back. Terminal\n  1500\t   state is data: re-stepping it is a no-op. `end` stops this\n  1501\t   interpreter and never closes a handle; a gap terminates (the\n  1502\t   terminal default policy — this adapter resumes nothing on its own).\"\n  1503\t  ([source destination state]\n  1504\t   (forward-step source destination state forward-default-options))\n  1505\t  ([source destination state options]\n  1506\t   (let [state (if (map? state) state {})\n  1507\t         options (merge forward-default-options (or options {}))\n  1508\t         status (:status state)\n  1509\t         budget (:batch-budget options)]\n  1510\t     (cond\n  1511\t       (and status (not (contains? #{:continue :retry} status)))\n  1512\t       state\n  1513\t\n  1514\t       (not (forward-budget-ok? budget))\n  1515\t       (forward-result {:cursor (:cursor state),\n  1516\t                        :frame (:frame state),\n  1517\t                        :pending (:pending state)}\n  1518\t                       :invalid-input\n  1519\t                       0\n  1520\t                       nil\n  1521\t                       {:rule :invalid-budget, :batch-budget budget})\n  1522\t\n  1523\t       :else\n  1524\t       (loop [cursor (:cursor state)\n  1525\t              frame (:frame state)\n  1526\t              pending (:pending state)\n  1527\t              remaining budget\n  1528\t              forwarded 0]\n  1529\t         (if (zero? remaining)\n  1530\t           (forward-result {:cursor cursor, :frame frame, :pending pending}\n  1531\t                           :continue\n  1532\t                           forwarded\n  1533\t                           nil\n  1534\t                           nil)\n  1535\t           (if (seq pending)\n  1536\t             (let [result (stream/append! destination (first pending))\n  1537\t                   outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n  1538\t               (case outcome\n  1539\t                 :dao.stream/ok\n  1540\t                 (recur cursor frame (rest pending) (dec remaining) (inc forwarded))\n  1541\t                 :dao.stream/full\n  1542\t                 (forward-result {:cursor cursor, :frame frame, :pending pending}\n  1543\t                                 :retry\n  1544\t                                 forwarded\n  1545\t                                 outcome\n  1546\t                                 nil)\n  1547\t                 (forward-result {:cursor cursor, :frame frame, :pending pending}\n  1548\t                                 (forward-destination-status outcome)\n  1549\t                                 forwarded\n  1550\t                                 outcome\n  1551\t                                 nil)))\n  1552\t             (let [result (stream/next source cursor)\n  1553\t                   outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)]\n  1554\t               (case outcome\n  1555\t                 :dao.stream/ok\n  1556\t                 ;; the try computes the successor frame; the recur stays\n  1557\t                 ;; outside it — a diagnostic is data, never a throw\n  1558\t                 (let [datum (:dao.stream/value result)\n  1559\t                       successor (:dao.stream/cursor result)\n  1560\t                       advanced (try\n  1561\t                                  (let [[_e a v] (check-datom datum)]\n  1562\t                                    (cond\n  1563\t                                      (and (= :yin/root a) (true? v))\n  1564\t                                      {:frame [],\n  1565\t                                       :pending (projected->datoms\n  1566\t                                                  (project-datoms (conj frame datum)))}\n  1567\t\n  1568\t                                      ;; datoms outside the :yin namespace\n  1569\t                                      ;; advance the cursor without extending\n  1570\t                                      ;; the frame, exactly as frame-datoms\n  1571\t                                      ;; frames them\n  1572\t                                      (not= \"yin\" (namespace a))\n  1573\t                                      {:frame frame, :pending pending}\n  1574\t\n  1575\t                                      :else {:frame (conj frame datum),\n     1\t(ns yin.vm.pipeline-test\n     2\t  \"D5 of docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md: the post-emission\n     3\t   pipeline that persists the named batch first and the projected envelope\n     4\t   second, independently — named failure skips projected persistence,\n     5\t   projection failure never fails the named side, dedupe is DaoJing's\n     6\t   write idempotence over the canonical envelope, and only complete\n     7\t   root-framed batches are projected.\"\n     8\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]])\n     9\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    10\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    11\t            [dao.jing.file :as jing-file]\n    12\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    13\t            [yin.vm.debruijn :as debruijn]\n    14\t            [yin.vm.pipeline :as pipeline]))\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\t;; =============================================================================\n    18\t;; Fixtures: a named writer and a DaoJing store, both owned by the test\n    19\t;; =============================================================================\n    20\t\n    21\t(defn- lit\n    22\t  [v]\n    23\t  {:type :literal, :value v})\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\t(defn- v\n    27\t  [s]\n    28\t  {:type :variable, :name s})\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t(defn- lam\n    32\t  [params body]\n    33\t  {:type :lambda, :params params, :body body})\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn- app\n    37\t  [op & args]\n    38\t  {:type :application, :operator op, :operands (vec args)})\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(def ^:private worked-example\n    42\t  (lam '[count] (app (v '+) (v 'count) (lit 1))))\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn- recording-writer\n    46\t  \"A named writer answering :ok with a transactor-shaped receipt and\n    47\t   recording every batch it accepted — and, given a shared event log,\n    48\t   logging [:named-write] there so its order against the store shows.\"\n    49\t  ([] (recording-writer nil))\n    50\t  ([log]\n    51\t   (let [batches (atom [])]\n    52\t     {:batches batches,\n    53\t      :writer (fn [datoms]\n    54\t                (swap! batches conj (vec datoms))\n    55\t                (when log (swap! log conj [:named-write]))\n    56\t                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n    57\t                 :dao.space/t 7,\n    58\t                 :dao.space/datoms (vec datoms)})})))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn- answering-writer\n    62\t  \"A named writer answering one fixed non-ok outcome, recording batches.\"\n    63\t  [outcome]\n    64\t  (let [batches (atom [])]\n    65\t    {:batches batches,\n    66\t     :writer (fn [datoms]\n    67\t               (swap! batches conj (vec datoms))\n    68\t               {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})}))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn- mem-store\n    72\t  \"The jing-test in-memory content store: :inserted on the first write of\n    73\t   an address, :present afterwards, never overwriting. The backing atom is\n    74\t   exposed as :store so the tests observe dedupe directly; given a shared\n    75\t   event log, every put logs [:put address result] and every get\n    76\t   [:get address].\"\n    77\t  ([] (mem-store nil))\n    78\t  ([log]\n    79\t   (let [store (atom {})\n    80\t         note! (fn [event] (when log (swap! log conj event)))]\n    81\t     (assoc {:store store}\n    82\t            :put-content-fn (fn [address payload]\n    83\t                              (let [result (if (contains? @store address)\n    84\t                                             :present\n    85\t                                             (do (swap! store assoc address payload)\n    86\t                                                 :inserted))]\n    87\t                                (note! [:put address result])\n    88\t                                result))\n    89\t            :get-content-fn (fn [address not-found]\n    90\t                              (note! [:get address])\n    91\t                              (if (contains? @store address)\n    92\t                                (get @store address)\n    93\t                                not-found))))))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn- refusing-store\n    97\t  \"A content store whose backend answers with an invalid result, so\n    98\t   materialize! throws.\"\n    99\t  []\n   100\t  {:put-content-fn (fn [_address _payload] :not-a-result),\n   101\t   :get-content-fn (fn [_address not-found] not-found)})\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn- persist!\n   105\t  ([ast]\n   106\t   (persist! ast (recording-writer) (mem-store)))\n   107\t  ([ast writer store]\n   108\t   (let [result (pipeline/persist-compiled! {:ast ast,\n   109\t                                             :named-writer (:writer writer),\n   110\t                                             :projected-store store,\n   111\t                                             :provenance {:batch :test}})]\n   112\t     (assoc result\n   113\t            :batches @(:batches writer)\n   114\t            :store-contents (when-let [backing (:store store)]\n   115\t                              @backing)))))\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t;; =============================================================================\n   119\t;; Separation and the happy path\n   120\t;; =============================================================================\n   121\t\n   122\t(deftest named-and-projected-persist-separately\n   123\t  (let [writer (recording-writer)\n   124\t        store (mem-store)\n   125\t        result (persist! worked-example writer store)\n   126\t        expected-datoms (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root worked-example))\n   127\t        address (get-in result [:projected :address])]\n   128\t    (is (= :ok (:outcome (:named result))))\n   129\t    (is (= [expected-datoms] (:batches result))\n   130\t        \"the named writer received the COMPLETE emission, root marker last\")\n   131\t    (is (= 7 (get-in result [:named :receipt :dao.space/t]))\n   132\t        \"the writer's own receipt rides under :receipt\")\n   133\t    (is (= :ok (:outcome (:projected result))))\n   134\t    (is (= (:fingerprint (debruijn/project-datoms expected-datoms))\n   135\t           (get-in result [:projected :fingerprint])))\n   136\t    (is (jing/segment-address? address))\n   137\t    (is (= {:yin.debruijn/fingerprint (get-in result [:projected :fingerprint]),\n   138\t            :yin.debruijn/datoms (debruijn/projected->datoms\n   139\t                                   (debruijn/project-datoms expected-datoms))}\n   140\t           (jing/get store address ::absent))\n   141\t        \"the store holds exactly the canonical envelope under its address\")\n   142\t    (is (= {:batch :test} (:provenance result))\n   143\t        \"provenance is echoed opaque, never interpreted\")\n   144\t    (is (not-any? #(= \"yin.debruijn\" (namespace (nth % 1))) (first (:batches result)))\n   145\t        \"no projected record entered the named batch — named datoms stay :yin/*\")\n   146\t    (is (every? #(= \"yin.debruijn\" (namespace (nth % 1)))\n   147\t                (:yin.debruijn/datoms (jing/get store address ::absent)))\n   148\t        \"the envelope's datoms are all :yin.debruijn/* — a separate segment\")))\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\t;; =============================================================================\n   152\t;; Failure isolation\n   153\t;; =============================================================================\n   154\t\n   155\t(deftest projection-failure-never-fails-the-named-side\n   156\t  (let [writer (recording-writer)\n   157\t        store (mem-store)\n   158\t        result (persist! (lam '[x] (app (v 'f) (lit (fn [q] q)))) writer store)]\n   159\t    (is (= :ok (:outcome (:named result))))\n   160\t    (is (= 1 (count (:batches result)))\n   161\t        \"the defective batch still persisted on the named side\")\n   162\t    (is (= :diagnostic (:outcome (:projected result))))\n   163\t    (is (= :unsupported-value (:rule (get-in result [:projected :diagnostic]))))\n   164\t    (is (empty? @(:store store))\n   165\t        \"no envelope was written for an unprojectable batch\")))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t(deftest projected-write-failure-is-reported-not-thrown\n   169\t  (let [writer (recording-writer)\n   170\t        result (persist! worked-example writer (refusing-store))]\n   171\t    (is (= :ok (:outcome (:named result))))\n   172\t    (is (= :diagnostic (:outcome (:projected result))))\n   173\t    (is (= :projected-write-failed (get-in result [:projected :diagnostic :rule])))\n   174\t    (is (= [:address :result]\n   175\t           (sort (keys (get-in result [:projected :diagnostic :cause])))))\n   176\t    (is (= :not-a-result (get-in result [:projected :diagnostic :cause :result]))\n   177\t        \"the store's answer rides under :cause — never the envelope payload\")))\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\t(deftest named-failure-skips-projected-persistence\n   181\t  (let [writer (answering-writer :dao.stream/full)\n   182\t        store (mem-store)\n   183\t        result (persist! worked-example writer store)]\n   184\t    (is (= :dao.stream/full (:outcome (:named result))))\n   185\t    (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full} (get-in result [:named :receipt])))\n   186\t    (is (= :not-attempted (:outcome (:projected result))))\n   187\t    (is (= :dao.stream/full (:named-outcome (:projected result))))\n   188\t    (is (empty? @(:store store))\n   189\t        \"projected persistence is never attempted after a named failure\")))\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t;; =============================================================================\n   193\t;; Dedupe: fingerprint identity, write-idempotent storage\n   194\t;; =============================================================================\n   195\t\n   196\t(deftest equal-projections-dedupe-to-one-envelope\n   197\t  (let [log (atom [])\n   198\t        writer (recording-writer log)\n   199\t        store (mem-store log)\n   200\t        first-result (persist! worked-example writer store)\n   201\t        second-result (persist! (lam '[n] (app (v '+) (v 'n) (lit 1))) writer store)\n   202\t        ;; snapshot before this test's own reads touch the store\n   203\t        events @log\n   204\t        address (get-in first-result [:projected :address])]\n   205\t    (is (= [[:named-write]\n   206\t            [:put address :inserted]\n   207\t            [:named-write]\n   208\t            [:put address :present]\n   209\t            [:get address]]\n   210\t           events)\n   211\t        \"the exact sequence: each named write precedes its store put, the\n   212\t         second put finds :present, and the only get is materialize!'s\n   213\t         read-back after :present — no pre-write lookup, no overwrite\")\n   214\t    (is (not-any? #(= :get (first %))\n   215\t                  (take-while #(not= :put (first %)) events))\n   216\t        \"no get precedes the first put\")\n   217\t    (is (= (get-in first-result [:projected :fingerprint])\n   218\t           (get-in second-result [:projected :fingerprint]))\n   219\t        \"alpha-equivalent programs share the Merkle fingerprint\")\n   220\t    (is (= (get-in first-result [:projected :address])\n   221\t           (get-in second-result [:projected :address]))\n   222\t        \"equal envelopes content-address to one segment\")\n   223\t    (is (= 1 (count @(:store store)))\n   224\t        \"the second write found :present: nothing overwritten, still one entry\")\n   225\t    (is (= 2 (count (:batches second-result)))\n   226\t        \"named artifacts are never deduplicated by fingerprint\")))\n   227\t\n   228\t\n   229\t(deftest different-programs-keep-different-identities\n   230\t  (let [one (persist! worked-example)\n   231\t        two (persist! (lam '[x] (v 'y)))]\n   232\t    (is (not= (get-in one [:projected :fingerprint])\n   233\t              (get-in two [:projected :fingerprint])))\n   234\t    (is (not= (get-in one [:projected :address])\n   235\t              (get-in two [:projected :address])))))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t;; =============================================================================\n   239\t;; Ordering: complete batches only, per-batch state\n   240\t;; =============================================================================\n   241\t\n   242\t(deftest partial-and-rootless-batches-reject-before-persistence\n   243\t  (let [writer (recording-writer)\n   244\t        store (mem-store)\n   245\t        complete (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root worked-example))\n   246\t        rootless (vec (butlast complete))\n   247\t        call (fn [datoms]\n   248\t               (pipeline/persist-compiled! {:datoms datoms,\n   249\t                                            :named-writer (:writer writer),\n   250\t                                            :projected-store store,\n   251\t                                            :provenance nil}))]\n   252\t    (testing \"a mid-emission prefix\"\n   253\t      (let [result (call rootless)]\n   254\t        (is (= :rejected (:outcome (:named result))))\n   255\t        (is (= :not-attempted (:outcome (:projected result))))\n   256\t        (is (= :partial-frame (:rule (:named result)) (:rule (:projected result)))\n   257\t            \"the rule is the framing gate's own\")))\n   258\t    (testing \"an entirely rootless batch\"\n   259\t      (let [result (call (filter #(not= :yin/root (nth % 1)) complete))]\n   260\t        (is (= :rejected (:outcome (:named result))))\n   261\t        (is (= :not-attempted (:outcome (:projected result)))))\n   262\t      (is (empty? @(:batches writer)) \"the writer was never called\")\n   263\t      (is (empty? @(:store store))\n   264\t          \"and nothing was ever projected\"))))\n   265\t\n   266\t\n   267\t(deftest only-exactly-one-complete-frame-persists\n   268\t  (let [complete (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root worked-example))\n   269\t        other (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root (lam '[x] (v 'y))))\n   270\t        retracting (mapv (fn [[e a val t :as d]]\n   271\t                           (if (= :yin/type a) [e a val t 0] d))\n   272\t                         complete)]\n   273\t    (doseq [[label datoms rule]\n   274\t            [[\"a complete graph trailed by an unfinished one\"\n   275\t              (into complete (butlast other))\n   276\t              :partial-frame]\n   277\t             [\"two concatenated complete graphs\"\n   278\t              (into complete other)\n   279\t              :multiple-frames]\n   280\t             [\"a retract datom\" retracting :retract]\n   281\t             [\"a malformed datom\" (conj complete [-16 :yin/type]) :malformed-datom]\n   282\t             [\"an empty batch\" [] :missing-root]]]\n   283\t      (testing label\n   284\t        (let [log (atom [])\n   285\t              writer (recording-writer log)\n   286\t              store (mem-store log)\n   287\t              result (pipeline/persist-compiled! {:datoms datoms,\n   288\t                                                  :named-writer (:writer writer),\n   289\t                                                  :projected-store store,\n   290\t                                                  :provenance nil})]\n   291\t          (is (= {:outcome :rejected, :rule rule} (:named result)))\n   292\t          (is (= {:outcome :not-attempted, :rule rule} (:projected result)))\n   293\t          (is (empty? @log) \"neither the writer nor the store was touched\"))))))\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\t(deftest writer-answers-without-a-keyword-outcome-are-classified\n   297\t  (doseq [answer [nil 5 {} {:dao.stream/outcome \"ok\"}]]\n   298\t    (let [store (mem-store)\n   299\t          result (pipeline/persist-compiled! {:ast worked-example,\n   300\t                                              :named-writer (fn [_] answer),\n   301\t                                              :projected-store store,\n   302\t                                              :provenance nil})]\n   303\t      (is (= {:outcome :invalid-writer-answer, :receipt answer} (:named result))\n   304\t          (str \"answer \" (pr-str answer)))\n   305\t      (is (= :not-attempted (:outcome (:projected result))))\n   306\t      (is (empty? @(:store store))))))\n   307\t\n   308\t\n   309\t(deftest a-request-takes-exactly-one-source\n   310\t  (let [writer (recording-writer)\n   311\t        rule-of (fn [request]\n   312\t                  (try (pipeline/persist-compiled! (merge {:named-writer (:writer writer),\n   313\t                                                           :projected-store (mem-store)}\n   314\t                                                          request))\n   315\t                       nil\n   316\t                       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n   317\t                         (:rule (ex-data e)))))]\n   318\t    (is (= :bad-request\n   319\t           (rule-of {:ast worked-example,\n   320\t                     :datoms (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root worked-example))}))\n   321\t        \"both :ast and :datoms\")\n   322\t    (is (= :bad-request (rule-of {})) \"neither\")\n   323\t    (is (empty? @(:batches writer)))))\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\t(deftest projection-defects-are-internal-errors-not-diagnostics\n   327\t  ;; no well-framed input reaches an internal defect, so one is injected by\n   328\t  ;; redefining the projection; :cljd first — ClojureDart does not redefine\n   329\t  ;; vars, and its host pass also reads :clj\n   330\t  #?(:cljd nil\n   331\t     :default (let [result (with-redefs [debruijn/project-datoms\n   332\t                                         (fn [_]\n   333\t                                           (throw (ex-info \"projection defect\"\n   334\t                                                           {:rule :missing-record})))]\n   335\t                             (persist! worked-example))]\n   336\t                (is (= :ok (:outcome (:named result))))\n   337\t                (is (= :internal-error (:outcome (:projected result))))\n   338\t                (is (= :internal-error (get-in result [:projected :diagnostic :rule])))\n   339\t                (is (= {:rule :missing-record}\n   340\t                       (get-in result [:projected :diagnostic :data])))))\n   341\t  (let [result (persist! (lam '[x] (app (v 'f) (lit (fn [q] q)))))]\n   342\t    (is (= :diagnostic (:outcome (:projected result)))\n   343\t        \"invalid input stays a :diagnostic, distinct from :internal-error\")))\n   344\t\n   345\t\n   346\t(deftest adjacent-batches-reusing-tempids-project-independently\n   347\t  (let [writer (recording-writer)\n   348\t        store (mem-store)\n   349\t        first-result (persist! worked-example writer store)\n   350\t        second-result (persist! worked-example writer store)]\n   351\t    (is (every? #(= :ok (:outcome %)) (map :projected [first-result second-result])))\n   352\t    (is (= (get-in first-result [:projected :address])\n   353\t           (get-in second-result [:projected :address]))\n   354\t        \"per-batch framing and index state: both -16-based emissions\n   355\t         project to the same one graph\")\n   356\t    (is (= 2 (count (:batches second-result)))\n   357\t        \"each call persisted its own named batch\")))\n   358\t\n   359\t\n   360\t;; =============================================================================\n   361\t;; D6 gaps: durable round trip and stored-tuple equality\n   362\t;; =============================================================================\n   363\t\n   364\t(defn- temp-path\n   365\t  []\n   366\t  (str \"target/test-pipeline-projected-\" (random-uuid) \".log\"))\n   367\t\n   368\t\n   369\t(defn- cleanup-file\n   370\t  \"Delete the file at path; :cljd first, since the ClojureDart host pass\n   371\t   also reads :clj.\"\n   372\t  [path]\n   373\t  #?(:cljd (try (let [f (dart-io/File. path)]\n   374\t                  (when (.existsSync f) (.deleteSync f)))\n   375\t                (catch Object _ nil))\n   376\t     :clj (let [f (java.io.File. path)] (when (.exists f) (.delete f)))\n   377\t     :cljs (try (.unlinkSync (js/require \"fs\") path) (catch :default _))))\n   378\t\n   379\t\n   380\t(deftest a-nil-literal-round-trips-through-durable-storage\n   381\t  (let [path (temp-path)\n   382\t        ast (lam '[x] (app (v 'f) (lit nil) (v 'x)))]\n   383\t    (try\n   384\t      (let [store (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   385\t            result (persist! ast (recording-writer) store)\n   386\t            address (get-in result [:projected :address])\n   387\t            _ (jing/close! store)\n   388\t            ;; reopen: the envelope now comes back through the backend's\n   389\t            ;; own text codec, replayed from disk\n   390\t            reopened (jing-file/create-content-file path)\n   391\t            stored (:yin.debruijn/datoms (jing/get reopened address ::absent))]\n   392\t        (jing/close! reopened)\n   393\t        (is (= :ok (:outcome (:projected result))))\n   394\t        (is (some (fn [d] (and (= :yin.debruijn/value (nth d 1)) (nil? (nth d 2))))\n   395\t                  stored)\n   396\t            \"the nil-valued datom survived storage as a present fact\")\n   397\t        (is (= (select-keys (debruijn/project-datoms\n   398\t                              (second (vm/ast->datoms-with-root ast)))\n   399\t                            [:fingerprint :records])\n   400\t               (debruijn/datoms->projected stored))\n   401\t            \"the reader verifies every stored record: no :hash-mismatch\"))\n   402\t      (finally (cleanup-file path)))))\n   403\t\n   404\t\n   405\t(deftest renamed-programs-store-equal-projected-datoms\n   406\t  (let [one-store (mem-store)\n   407\t        two-store (mem-store)\n   408\t        one (persist! worked-example (recording-writer) one-store)\n   409\t        two (persist! (lam '[n] (app (v '+) (v 'n) (lit 1))) (recording-writer) two-store)\n   410\t        stored (fn [store result]\n   411\t                 (:yin.debruijn/datoms\n   412\t                   (jing/get store (get-in result [:projected :address]) ::absent)))]\n   413\t    (is (seq (stored one-store one)))\n   414\t    (is (= (stored one-store one) (stored two-store two))\n   415\t        \"two separate stores hold the identical projected tuples for an\n   416\t         alpha-equivalent pair\")))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
